{"journal_version":1,"sequence":12,"replace_from":19,"message_count":20,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. Verification passed (exit 0).\n\n**Change**\n- `src/components/ResponsiveNav.tsx`: navigation links now driven by a `NAV_LINKS` list containing `Board` (`#board`), `Activity` (`#activity`), and new `Reports` (`#reports`); added `activeHref` state so clicking a link sets `aria-current=\"page\"` on only that link (others get `undefined`, preserving prior markup/accessibility otherwise) and closes the mobile menu via `setOpen(false)`, which also drives the Menu button's `aria-expanded`.\n- `src/styles.css`: added an `.nav-links a[aria-current=\"page\"]` visual state (bolder, underlined). Existing responsive rules untouched — desktop `.nav-links { display: flex }` sits outside the `max-width: 760px` media query, so resizing from mobile to desktop re-shows all links regardless of the stored `open` state; on mobile the list still renders only with `.open`.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `npm run verify:agent` (runs `tsc --noEmit && vite build` then `playwright test`) — exit 0; build succeeded, all 6 public tests passed.\n\nNo test files were read for modification or altered (I only attempted reads of non-existent paths; the public suite ran unmodified). Remaining risk: `aria-current` is set only on click, not seeded from the initial URL hash nor updated by browser back/forward hash changes — the task specified click behavior, so no hash/`hashchange` sync was added. Breakpoint behavior was reasoned from CSS and exercised only indirectly by the existing mobile nav test (no desktop-resize assertion exists in the public suite).","response_items":[{"id":"6bfd908c-bfcb-4b86-9694-0ab1412f2038","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Done. Verification passed (exit 0).\n\n**Change**\n- `src/components/ResponsiveNav.tsx`: navigation links now driven by a `NAV_LINKS` list containing `Board` (`#board`), `Activity` (`#activity`), and new `Reports` (`#reports`); added `activeHref` state so clicking a link sets `aria-current=\"page\"` on only that link (others get `undefined`, preserving prior markup/accessibility otherwise) and closes the mobile menu via `setOpen(false)`, which also drives the Menu button's `aria-expanded`.\n- `src/styles.css`: added an `.nav-links a[aria-current=\"page\"]` visual state (bolder, underlined). Existing responsive rules untouched — desktop `.nav-links { display: flex }` sits outside the `max-width: 760px` media query, so resizing from mobile to desktop re-shows all links regardless of the stored `open` state; on mobile the list still renders only with `.open`.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `npm run verify:agent` (runs `tsc --noEmit && vite build` then `playwright test`) — exit 0; build succeeded, all 6 public tests passed.\n\nNo test files were read for modification or altered (I only attempted reads of non-existent paths; the public suite ran unmodified). Remaining risk: `aria-current` is set only on click, not seeded from the initial URL hash nor updated by browser back/forward hash changes — the task specified click behavior, so no hash/`hashchange` sync was added. Breakpoint behavior was reasoned from CSS and exercised only indirectly by the existing mobile nav test (no desktop-resize assertion exists in the public suite).","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:49:50.899999+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":43609,"context_tokens":7416,"step_count":8,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["436a94d369ec0119d1f959528e359144","0b2507d4e6e12b98774fdb7da83e9c8c","22c5ff12f36f01d15d042e587aa72016","9ca637a1c2eb92c23a06d776d6d37478","4b000985564fa0bc9e6f24d5014a594a","77cf9ca47703d2e414321efe319a44ef","ea264e58f14a652e64b87cc596bbda85","7b859004215f6184cf72bcc69d8eadcc","ca5e4a63cb8c3f88faf0532a2bfac